## Overview

Go module: `{{ .module_name }}`

## Git & Pull Requests

- **Conventional commits**: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `ci:`, `test:`
  (`!` for breaking changes).
- **Signing & DCO**: sign commits and include a DCO `Signed-off-by:` trailer
  (`git commit -s -S`).
- **Squash-merge repository**: every PR becomes one commit on `main` built from
  the **PR title and body** (`PR_TITLE` / `PR_BODY`). Keep the PR title a valid
  conventional-commit subject and update the PR body whenever a new commit
  changes what the PR does.
- **Copilot review discipline**: Copilot reviews ready-for-review PRs on open
  (`review_on_push: false`). Wait for CI checks to pass before requesting a
  re-review, and only re-request Copilot after pushing fixes for open findings.

## Build, Test & Lint

~~~bash
{{- if .include_go_ci }}
# Install missing CI tools (golangci-lint, gosec) into .tool/bin
scafctl run action install-tools -f ./ci/go-ci/actions.yaml

# Run full portable Go CI locally (gofmt, vet, lint, gosec, race tests, coverage, build)
scafctl run action ci -f ./ci/go-ci/actions.yaml

{{- end }}
# Run targeted Go tests during iteration
go test -race ./...
~~~

## Go Conventions

- Wrap errors with context and `%w` (`fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`), preserve
  `errors.Is` / `errors.As`, and never panic in library packages.
- Maintain **{{ .min_coverage }}%+ statement coverage** with table-driven tests
  exercising public interfaces rather than private internals.
- Close opened files, network bodies, and goroutines cleanly; respect
  `context.Context` cancellation.
- Never commit secrets, credentials, or user-specific home paths (such as
  `/home/<user>/` or `/Users/<user>/`).
